    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334-a1">

                <pb facs="0406" n="1140" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1140"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Schmidt to the Consuls.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mulinuu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: In continuation of my letters of
                    December 29, 1894, and January 30,1895, concerning the Samoan finances, I have
                    the honor to transmit to you copies of the latest Government resolutions in
                    reply to my estimate of this year’s receipts and expenses.</p>
                <p>I should thank you for kindly forwarding also this document to your Governments,
                    to serve as an illustration of the consequences resulting from Chief Justice
                    Ide’s decision on the rights and duties of the Samoan treasurer.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Schmidt</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >President.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
